<title>USA: Arco says no crude oil limits on Line 63.</title>
<headline>Arco says no crude oil limits on Line 63.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1996-12-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Atlantic Richfield's Arco Pipeline Co said on Tuesday it would not prorate January crude oil shipments on its California Line 63.</p>
<p>&quot;We'll move all the oil that shippers desire,&quot; said a Arco Pipeline spokesman.</p>
<p>The company said it set no limits on its December shipments.</p>
<p>Crude shipments on Line 63, which runs from California's San Joaquin Valley to Los Angeles, have been limited since a January 1994 earthquake knocked out a companion line.</p>
